---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, withBase } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="A Midwestern family physician writing about medicine, life, and the occasional well-made drink.">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 44rem">
    <p class="kicker" style="color: var(--amber)">The masthead</p>
    <h1 style="font-family: var(--serif-display); font-size: clamp(2rem,5vw,3.2rem); letter-spacing:-0.03em; margin: 0 0 0.8rem;">About</h1>
    <div class="prose" style="margin: 0; padding: 0; max-width: none">
      <p>
        I’m a Midwestern family physician — board-certified — who still believes medicine is
        mostly about people. The work is to listen well, help when I can, and treat patients
        like neighbors, not charts.
      </p>
      <p>
        Away from clinic I try to stay curious: new places with family, ordinary days that turn
        out better than expected, and the small fine things that make a week feel like a life.
        Sometimes that is a quiet evening and a well-balanced cocktail. Not as an escape —
        just as one more way to pay attention.
      </p>
      <p>
        I write here as <strong>{SITE.author}</strong>. The essays are candid and imperfect.
        If a story touches a patient, the details stay general on purpose.
      </p>
      <p>
        Comments need an email (never published) and go for review before anything appears.
        You can also find me on X at
        <a href={SITE.twitter} rel="me noopener">{SITE.twitterHandle}</a>,
        or subscribe via <a href={withBase('rss.xml')}>RSS</a>.
        Linking is welcome; republishing is not.
      </p>
      <p><em>{SITE.copyright}</em></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
